IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`

-- Tests for subsection (a) and for the span arithmetic it rests on.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the calendar and the text, then run; none was copied from the output.
-- Sale on 15 March 2026. The 5-year period is 16 March 2021 to 15 March 2026 (365 + 365 + 366 + 365 + 365 = 1826 days; 29 February 2024 is inside it).
-- 2 years ending on that date: 16 March 2024 to 15 March 2026 = 730 days (29 February 2024 falls before 16 March 2024).

§ `Tests: subsection (a)`

`a test sale date` MEANS Date 15 3 2026
`a test window` MEANS `s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` `a test sale date`

#ASSERT `a test window`'s `first day` EQUALS Date 16 3 2021
#ASSERT `a test window`'s `last day` EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `the days in the span` `a test window` EQUALS 1826
#ASSERT `s 121(a) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` `a test sale date` EQUALS 730

-- A sale on 29 February: 5 years earlier is 29 February 2019, which does not exist and rolls to 1 March 2019; the period starts the day after.
#ASSERT (`s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` (Date 29 2 2024))'s `first day` EQUALS Date 2 3 2019
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (`s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` (Date 29 2 2024)) EQUALS 1826

-- The ownership requirement: exactly 2 years (730 days) meets it, 729 days does not.
`a test owned 730 days` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 16 3 2024), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a test owned 729 days` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 17 3 2024), (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` `a test owned 730 days` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` `a test owned 729 days` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Periods aggregate: two separate years, 365 + 365 = 730, meet it; 365 + 364 = 729 does not.
`a test two spans 730` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 16 3 2021), (Date 15 3 2022)
    Span OF (Date 16 3 2025), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a test two spans 729` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 16 3 2021), (Date 15 3 2022)
    Span OF (Date 17 3 2025), (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the use requirement is met` `a test two spans 730` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the use requirement is met` `a test two spans 729` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Only days inside the 5-year period count: a span that starts in 2019 counts from 16 March 2021.
`a test long span ends 15 3 2023` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2019), (Date 15 3 2023)
`a test long span ends 14 3 2023` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2019), (Date 14 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` `a test long span ends 15 3 2023` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` `a test long span ends 14 3 2023` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Subsection (g) adds days: 729 days of use and 1 day included under (g) meet the requirement; with none included they do not.
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the use requirement is met` `a test owned 729 days` `a test window` `a test sale date` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the use requirement is met` `a test owned 729 days` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Both requirements: met only when each is met (read of (a) at fork F1: they need not coincide in time).
`a test holding both` MEANS Holding OF `a test owned 730 days`, `a test owned 730 days`
`a test holding use short` MEANS Holding OF `a test owned 730 days`, `a test owned 729 days`
`a test holding owned short` MEANS Holding OF `a test owned 729 days`, `a test owned 730 days`
`a test holding neither` MEANS Holding OF `a test owned 729 days`, `a test owned 729 days`
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` `a test holding both` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` `a test holding use short` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` `a test holding owned short` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` `a test holding neither` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The operative sentence of (a).
#ASSERT `s 121(a) gross income does not include the gain` `a test holding both` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 121(a) gross income does not include the gain` `a test holding neither` `a test window` `a test sale date` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests: the span arithmetic`

-- the days in a span, both ends counted
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 1 1 2020)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020)) EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (Span OF (Date 2 1 2020), (Date 1 1 2020)) EQUALS 0

-- the overlap
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (`the overlap of the spans` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 1 2020)) (Span OF (Date 16 1 2020), (Date 15 2 2020))) EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `the days in the span` (`the overlap of the spans` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 1 2020)) (Span OF (Date 1 2 2020), (Date 15 2 2020))) EQUALS 0

-- a span less a span: a span in the middle leaves two pieces; a disjoint span leaves it whole; a covering span leaves nothing
`a test month` MEANS Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 1 2020)
#ASSERT count (`the span less the span` `a test month` (Span OF (Date 11 1 2020), (Date 20 1 2020))) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s) (`the span less the span` `a test month` (Span OF (Date 11 1 2020), (Date 20 1 2020)))) EQUALS 21
#ASSERT count (`the span less the span` `a test month` (Span OF (Date 1 3 2020), (Date 20 3 2020))) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`the span less the span` `a test month` (Span OF (Date 1 12 2019), (Date 31 1 2020))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the days in the span` s) (`the span less the span` `a test month` (Span OF (Date 20 1 2020), (Date 28 2 2020)))) EQUALS 19

-- the union counts a day once: a month and an overlapping fortnight make 31 + 14 - 16 ... see the numbers below
`a test fortnight` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 25 1 2020), (Date 7 2 2020)
#ASSERT `the days of the spans inside the window` (`the spans of both lists` (LIST `a test month`) `a test fortnight`) (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020)) EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `the days of the spans inside the window` (`the spans of both lists` (LIST `a test month`) (LIST `a test month`)) (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020)) EQUALS 31

-- the days in both lists
#ASSERT `the days in both lists inside the window` (LIST `a test month`) `a test fortnight` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 12 2020)) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the days in both lists inside the window` (LIST `a test month`) `a test fortnight` (Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 28 1 2020)) EQUALS 4

-- N years ending on / beginning with
#ASSERT `the days in the years ending on` (Date 15 3 2025) 1 EQUALS 365
-- 1 year ending on 15 March 2024 starts 16 March 2023, so it holds 29 February 2024: 366 days; ending on 15 March 2025 it starts 16 March 2024, after the leap day: 365.
#ASSERT `the days in the years ending on` (Date 15 3 2024) 1 EQUALS 366
#ASSERT (`the span of the years beginning with` (Date 15 3 2024) 5)'s `last day` EQUALS Date 14 3 2029
#ASSERT `the date years after` (Date 29 2 2024) 2 EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date is in the span` (Date 31 1 2020) `a test month`
#ASSERT NOT (`the date is in the span` (Date 1 2 2020) `a test month`)

-- the latest last day; the spans latest first
`a test mixed spans` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 1 2020)
    Span OF (Date 1 6 2020), (Date 2 6 2020)
    Span OF (Date 1 3 2020), (Date 2 3 2020)
`a test mixed spans latest first` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 1 6 2020), (Date 2 6 2020)
    Span OF (Date 1 3 2020), (Date 2 3 2020)
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2020), (Date 31 1 2020)
#ASSERT `the latest last day of the spans` `a test fortnight` EQUALS JUST (Date 7 2 2020)
#ASSERT `the latest last day of the spans` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the latest last day of the spans` `a test mixed spans` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 6 2020)
#ASSERT `the spans latest first` `a test mixed spans` EQUALS `a test mixed spans latest first`

-- the three-valued logic
#ASSERT `both are true` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `both are true` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `both are true` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `both are true` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `both are true` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `both are true` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `either is true` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `either is true` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `either is true` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `either is true` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `either is true` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the opposite of` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the opposite of` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
